      "text": "I saw a man … dressed in a white robe, 1 Ne. 8:5 (14:19; 3 Ne. 11:8; JS—H 1:32). I beheld that the fruit thereof was white, 1 Ne. 8:11. I beheld a virgin … fair and white, 1 Ne. 11:13 (13:15; 2 Ne. 5:21). garments are made white in his blood, 1 Ne. 12:10 (Alma 5:27; 13:11–12; 34:36; Ether 13:10; D&C 20:6). he denieth none that come unto him, black and white, 2 Ne. 26:33. unless ye shall repent … their skins will be whiter than yours, Jacob 3:8. can no man be saved except his garments are washed white, Alma 5:21. whose garments are … pure and white, Alma 5:24. pluck the fruit thereof … which is white above all that is white, Alma 32:42. their skin became white, 3 Ne. 2:15. thou canst not make one hair black or white, 3 Ne. 12:36. they were as white as the countenance … of Jesus, 3 Ne. 19:25. that perhaps ye may be found … fair, and white, Morm. 9:6. sixteen small stones … white and clear, Ether 3:1.",
